<title>UK: Texaco, Gulf face refinery fire charges on Friday.</title>
<headline>Texaco, Gulf face refinery fire charges on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.K.'s safety watchdog said it will begin prosecution of Texaco Ltd and Chevron Corp unit Gulf Oil (Great Britain) Ltd on Friday following an explosion and fire at their Pembroke oil refinery in July 1994.</p>
<p>The explosion and fire caused extensive damage to the plant, 26 people were injured, none seriously, and there was also damage to properties nearby.</p>
<p>Each company will face two charges from the Health and Safety Executive which allege that, as partners in Pembroke Cracking Company, they failed to ensure, so far as was reasonably practicable, the safety of employees, sub-contractors and members of the public.</p>
<p>The case is due to be heard at Swansea in Wales.</p>
